# --- Quarto ---
**/.quarto/
/.quarto/
/_site*/
/_book*/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
**/*.rmarkdown
**/mathjax-config.js
/.luarc.json

# _freeze/ is versioned for its per-doc execute-results/*.json — the R compute cache, the core of
# freeze that lets CI reuse results without re-running R. Its site_libs/ are regenerable and NOT
# meant to be committed (confirmed against quarto-cli via DeepWiki): Quarto repopulates them from
# its own install on every render, and they aren't strictly required for a no-engine render — so
# committing them is just ~5 MB of churn. Keep them out of git.
# Note: site_libs/ can also carry htmlwidget (plotly/leaflet) libs; per DeepWiki still not strictly
# required off-engine — but if a frozen widget ever fails to load on CI, un-ignore / track its lib.
/_freeze/site_libs/

# Stray render libs written next to source when a single file is rendered outside the site build
# (the site build puts them in _site/site_libs/). Regenerable — never commit.
/site_libs/

# Per-doc figure working dirs written next to source on render (typst needs the figure on disk).
# Quarto restores these from _freeze/ — the canonical frozen copies live under _freeze/. Not sources.
**/*_files/
# SVGs emitted by typst-render (output-directory: typst-figures). Regenerated on every render and
# published from _site/ — never committed (matches tuto-quarto-typst-rr-2026).
**/typst-figures/
# Composed Typst source from keep-typ, if ever re-enabled — a build artifact, not a source.
**/*.typ
# knitr intermediate written next to source on render (e.g. by a reviewer verifying a page).
# Regenerated on every render; the frozen results live under _freeze/. Not a source.
**/*.knit.md
# Rendered HTML written next to source when a single .qmd is rendered outside the project
# (the site build puts pages in _site/). HTML is always generated here, never a source.
**/*.html

# --- R ---
.Rproj.user/
**/.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# --- braid (issue tracker) — the doc id in .braid.toml is a bearer token ---
.braid.toml
.braid-stragglers.jsonl

# --- local visual-review tooling (Playwright screenshots; never committed) ---
/.review-shots/
/node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
.positai

# --- throwaway repo clones used by review agents (do NOT commit; clean after) ---
/rr-2023/
/typst-rr-2026/
/user2024-talk/
/user2024-tutorial/
/raukr-2025-quarto/
/raukr-2025/
/raukr-2026/
